<title>FRANCE: MOTORCYCLING-SUZUKI WINS LE MANS 24 HOURS ENDURANCE RACE.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-SUZUKI WINS LE MANS 24 HOURS ENDURANCE RACE.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suzuki won Le Mans 24 Hours race, the opening stage of the motorcycling endurance world championship on Sunday.</p>
<p>Suzuki, teaming Juan-Eric Gomez of France, Doug Polen of the United States and Peter Goddard of Australia, clinched their fourth win on the famous Bugatti track.</p>
<p>Suzuki's last win here was in 1985.</p>
